    "title": "McMenamins Edgefield marks 115 years of brews, fun and storied history - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Emily Burris Mia Villanueva ,\n9 hours ago\nPORTLAND, Ore. ( KOIN ) – An iconic property in Troutdale that has seen dramatic transformation over the years is marking a major milestone.\nMcMenamins Edgefield is celebrating its 115th birthday on Saturday, July 11, and the company is inviting the public to join the party.\nClose Thanks for signing up!\nWatch for us in your inbox.\nSubscribe Now\nKOIN Morning Digest The facility was originally built in 1911 and served as a “poor farm” for seven decades, hosting a variety of people who needed a leg up in life, including sea captains, teachers, ministers, musicians, nurses, former slaves and more.\nMcMenamins’ history department manager Jon Smart and tour guide manager Caitlin Popp joined us on AM Extra to look back at 115 years of fun, brews, food, live music, hospitality and storied history.\nWatch the full story in the video player above.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KOIN.com.\n2",
    "summary": "By Emily Burris Mia Villanueva , PORTLAND, Ore. ( KOIN ) – An iconic property in Troutdale that has seen dramatic transformation over the years is marking a major milestone. McMenamins Edgefield is celebrating its 115th birthday on Saturday, July 11, and the company is inviting the public to join the party. KOIN Morning Digest The facility was originally built in 1911 and served as a “poor farm” for seven decades, hosting a variety of people who needed a leg up in life, including sea captains, teachers, ministers, musicians, nurses, former slaves and more.",
